 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "$\\Pic$, degree, $\\Pic^0$",
 "statement": "Let $C$ be a scheme over a field $k$. We write $\\Pic(C)$ for the set of\ninvertible $\\cO_C$-modules up to isomorphism (for $C$ a smooth projective\ngeometrically integral curve this is the group $H^1(C_{\\Et},\\gm)$). The\n*degree* of a class is $\\deg\\cL:=\\chi(C,\\cL)-\\chi(C,\\cO_C)$, and\n$\\Pic^0(C):=\\{\\cL\\in\\Pic(C):\\deg\\cL=0\\}$. For a field extension $K/k$ we\nwrite $C_K=C\\times_kK$ and $\\Pic^0(C_K)$ for the degree-zero part over $K$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-def-av-pic/_section.md",
